<section>
  <div class="wrap with-aside">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>All the freedom of a private yacht, none of the hassle</h2>
      <p class="lead">Paddle a glassy cove at sunrise. Walk through old growth cedar. Watch for whales from the flybridge. Sit down to Northwest seafood at anchor.</p>
      <p>A private charter gives your group the whole of Supernova with Captain Paul and a mate. We'll plan the route with you, from the San Juan Islands to the Gulf Islands, Desolation Sound and beyond.</p>

      <h2>What you can do</h2>
      <ul class="checklist cols-2">
        <li>Paddleboard and kayak quiet anchorages</li>
        <li>Hike island trails and old growth forest</li>
        <li>Go ashore by tender or landing craft</li>
        <li>Watch for whales, seals, porpoises and eagles</li>
        <li>Dive with an added divemaster</li>
        <li>Swim, fish and explore beaches</li>
        <li>Eat Northwest cuisine from a private chef</li>
        <li>Or just slow down and do nothing</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">Wildlife sightings are never guaranteed, and stops always depend on weather and conditions.</p>

      <h2>Ways to charter</h2>
      <h3>Culinary voyages</h3>
      <p>Add a private chef for Northwest inspired whole food meals with local seafood and seasonal ingredients, served with views. Paddle, hike or relax between courses.</p>
      <h3>Corporate retreats</h3>
      <p>Take your team off the grid. Supernova is remote, inspiring and entirely yours, a place to unplug, think clearly and build real camaraderie.</p>
      <h3>Family trips and celebrations</h3>
      <p>Milestone birthdays, anniversaries and family reunions. Tell us the occasion and we'll plan the trip around it.</p>
      <h3>Dry boat charters</h3>
      <p>For licensed, experienced captains. Take the helm of Supernova yourself after pre qualification and a full vessel orientation. Captain Paul is on call 24/7 throughout your charter.</p>
      <h3>Dry boat charter with skipper coaching</h3>
      <p>Aspiring skipper? Charter Supernova with Captain Paul as your mentor and build real experience in navigation, route planning, anchoring and systems while your family enjoys the islands.</p>

      <h2>Who it's for</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Families and friends who want the boat to themselves</li>
        <li>Food lovers who want a culinary voyage</li>
        <li>Teams looking for a different kind of retreat</li>
        <li>Experienced boaters ready to skipper a 78 foot yacht</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Charter questions</h2>
      <div class="faq" data-faq-schema>
        <details><summary>How many people can come?</summary><p>Crewed private charters are limited to 6 paying guests under U.S. Coast Guard rules. Dry boat charters can sleep 8 in the staterooms plus up to 4 more on the top deck.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is food included?</summary><p>The base charter is self catered. Add a private chef for chef prepared meals with house beer, wine and standard spirits.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do we have to start in Anacortes?</summary><p>All trips start and end in Anacortes, WA. Alternative pickup and drop off locations are available for an added fuel charge.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can we go into Canada?</summary><p>Yes. Longer charters regularly cross into British Columbia's Gulf Islands. Every guest needs valid travel documents for entering Canada and returning to the U.S.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside id="details" style="scroll-margin-top:110px">
      <div class="details">
        <h3>Charter details</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>Price</dt><dd>$3,900 per night, whole boat with Captain and Mate</dd>
          <dt>Length</dt><dd>2 nights minimum, up to 30 days</dd>
          <dt>Guests</dt><dd>Up to 6</dd>
          <dt>Departs</dt><dd>Anacortes, WA</dd>
          <dt>Included</dt><dd>Captain and mate, 4 paddleboards, 2 kayaks, 15 foot tender</dd>
          <dt>Add ons</dt><dd>Private chef from $800/night, landing craft $500/night, divemaster $500/night</dd>
        </dl>
        {{ book(site, "/calendar/?trip=private#request") }}
